---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
import katex from 'katex'

const architecture = katex.renderToString(
  String.raw`\mathcal C_{\mathrm{Car}}\xrightarrow{\mathsf K_s}\mathcal D_s\xrightarrow{\mathsf R_s}\mathcal O_s`,
  { displayMode: true, throwOnError: false },
)
const pairedRuntime = katex.renderToString(
  String.raw`\text{shared geometric microkernel}+\{(\text{coefficient system},\text{physical readout})_s\}`,
  { displayMode: true, throwOnError: false },
)
const constructorConjecture = katex.renderToString(
  String.raw`\text{possible task}=\text{Carrier-typed transformation}+\text{coherent resources}+\text{repeatable readout}`,
  { displayMode: true, throwOnError: false },
)
const relationalView = katex.renderToString(
  String.raw`\text{identity--relation substrate}\xrightarrow{\text{typed sector view}}\text{operational alternatives}\xrightarrow{\text{state}}\operatorname{Prob}(\Omega)`,
  { displayMode: true, throwOnError: false },
)
const entropyRefinement = katex.renderToString(
  String.raw`H(\Omega')=H(\Omega)+\sum_{\omega\in\Omega}p(\omega)H(\Omega'_\omega)`,
  { displayMode: true, throwOnError: false },
)
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Speculations · Marici"
  description="Explicitly conjectural architectural interpretations suggested by Marici's established research record."
>
  <section class="section-shell" aria-labelledby="speculations-title">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Speculations</p>
        <h1 id="speculations-title">Ideas worth sharpening, not results to inherit.</h1>
      </div>
      <p>
        This section records architectural interpretations suggested by the research program. Each
        speculation separates its evidence, conjectural step, falsifier, and prohibited overclaim.
        The <a href="/frontier/">Frontier Atlas</a>, epistemic graph, and Ledger remain the evidence-bearing records.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="frontier-card frontier-card--gap" aria-labelledby="microkernel-title">
      <header>
        <p>Speculation 01 · architectural analogy</p>
        <span>conjectural</span>
      </header>
      <h2 id="microkernel-title">One geometric microkernel, many typed runtimes</h2>
      <div class="formula" aria-label="Carrier to coefficient to observable architecture" set:html={architecture}></div>
      <p>
        The recurring carrier–coefficient–selection separation resembles a typed microkernel.
        The shared Carrier supplies a small calculus of legal incidence, degeneration, support,
        transport, and comparison operations. A sector contributes a coefficient system and a
        physical readout that together behave like a typed runtime and its interpreter.
      </p>
      <div class="formula" aria-label="Shared geometric microkernel plus sector runtime pairs" set:html={pairedRuntime}></div>
    </article>

    <div class="dimension-grid" aria-label="Status and tests for speculation 01">
      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Established pressure</p>
        <h2>Three stages repeatedly separate</h2>
        <p>
          Across cosmology, flavor, strings, and radiative gravity, carrier incidence, coefficient
          classes, and physical activation cannot be substituted for one another. Nonzero internal
          data does not guarantee a physical observable.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Conjectural step</p>
        <h2>The runtime may be the pair</h2>
        <p>
          A coefficient object may acquire its operational meaning only together with its allowed
          readout. The sector-specific unit could therefore be the pair
          <code>(coefficient system, physical readout)</code>, rather than either component alone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Sharp falsifiers</p>
        <h2>Break the shared kernel or split the pair</h2>
        <p>
          The analogy fails if a sector requires a structural operation not generated by the shared
          Carrier calculus. Its stronger paired-runtime form fails if a coefficient object has the
          same canonical operational meaning under genuinely different physical readouts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Non-claims</p>
        <h2>No literal software ontology</h2>
        <p>
          This does not claim that nature is software, that the Carrier is a computer, or that
          physical observers are forced by human perception to use one runtime. Those are separate
          hypotheses requiring independent evidence.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <article class="frontier-card frontier-card--gap" aria-labelledby="deutsch-popper-title">
      <header>
        <p>Speculation 02 · possibility and falsifiability</p>
        <span>conjectural</span>
      </header>
      <h2 id="deutsch-popper-title">The Deutsch–Popperian Conjecture</h2>
      <p>
        The Carrier may encode a constructor-theoretic possibility structure: not merely which
        configurations exist, but which transformations can be performed repeatedly using
        source-admissible resources. Popperian discipline enters through severe failure tests:
        incidence, descent, support, horizontality, and physical selection must be derived before
        a proposed task is called possible.
      </p>
      <div class="formula" aria-label="Constructor-theoretic possibility criterion" set:html={constructorConjecture}></div>
    </article>

    <div class="dimension-grid" aria-label="Status and tests for the Deutsch–Popperian Conjecture">
      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Conjectural translation</p>
        <h2>Coherence supplies the constructor</h2>
        <p>
          A labelled local operation is only a presentation. It becomes a possible task when an
          incidence- and descent-coherent complex transports it, composes it, and exposes a
          supported readout without adding untyped choices.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">First severe test</p>
        <h2>Five-site OFPT primitives</h2>
        <p>
          Independent linear numerators saturate the finite evaluation oracle. The conjecture
          predicts that the source-derived OFPT incidence/Koszul complex selects a smaller,
          composable primitive space. The first naïve realization already fails: the declared
          unit-weight 180-term OFPT sum is not a cycle in the abstract four-facet incidence
          complex, and no unrestricted or cyclically invariant unit-magnitude signing repairs it.
          The stronger rational exclusion was wrong: after including the orientation sign induced
          by cyclic transport, a nine-dimensional invariant cycle space survives and meets every
          term orbit. Reflection splits it into six even and three odd directions. Source symmetry
          does not choose a vector, but the signed denominator determinant supplies a canonical
          invariant covector: it annihilates the odd sector and defines a rank-one quotient of the
          even sector. The 180 terms still cannot be reinterpreted as matroid bases—58,010 of
          102,920 basis-exchange obligations fail. The first physical-map test is negative: the
          generic deck-traced OFPT rational function detects all six even directions, all five
          determinant-null directions, and all three odd directions. Thus the determinant is a
          canonical combinatorial augmentation, not yet a physical readout. Only a separately
          derived integration-chain or supported quotient could still remove the extra directions.
          The determinant-character quotient persists exactly from triangles through hexagons;
          however, the matching possibility-space dimensions 1, 2, 6, and 38 already falsify the
          tempting factorial extrapolation at six sites.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Cross-sector prediction</p>
        <h2>One obstruction vocabulary</h2>
        <p>
          Missing Beck–Chevalley cells, nonhorizontal quotients, failed weak-basis descent, and
          absent physical pairings should all admit one resource-sensitive account of impossible
          composition—not merely analogous descriptions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Prohibited overclaim</p>
        <h2>No constructor ontology yet</h2>
        <p>
          This does not establish constructor theory as fundamental physics, identify human
          perception with a readout, or prove that every obstruction is an impossibility law.
          Those claims require new invariants and independent tests.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <article class="frontier-card frontier-card--gap" aria-labelledby="relational-view-title">
      <header>
        <p>Speculation 03 · relational substrate and entropy</p>
        <span>conjectural</span>
      </header>
      <h2 id="relational-view-title">Identity, typed relations, and operational views</h2>
      <p>
        The emerging architecture resembles an event-sourced entity–relation system. Primitive
        identities record available distinctions; typed relations record incidence, equivalence,
        refinement, support, and composition. Sector lenses and physical readouts behave like
        governed queries or materialized views over that substrate—but the analogy is structural,
        not a claim that nature literally runs a database.
      </p>
      <div
        class="formula"
        aria-label="Identity relation substrate to operational probability view"
        set:html={relationalView}
      ></div>
      <p>
        A stored row, graph node, or algebraic summand is not automatically a physical alternative.
        It counts only when a source-derived effect can distinguish it. Once a sector supplies a
        finite positive normalized state and coherent refinements of its operational alternatives,
        Shannon entropy is the additive refinement valuation.
      </p>
      <div
        class="formula"
        aria-label="Shannon grouping law on an operational refinement"
        set:html={entropyRefinement}
      ></div>
    </article>

    <div class="dimension-grid" aria-label="Status and tests for the relational substrate speculation">
      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Established pressure</p>
        <h2>Two manifestations and one negative control</h2>
        <p>
          Fixed-kinematics scattering and weak-basis-invariant flavor overlap independently
          generate canonical probability states. The positive cosmological period does not:
          symmetry-preserving refinement leaves its scalar value fixed while shifting a proposed
          entropy by <code>log 2</code>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Conjectural step</p>
        <h2>Views may be generated, not imposed</h2>
        <p>
          A common identity–relation substrate may co-generate each sector’s coefficient lens,
          physical readout, and allowed refinement maps. Entropy would then manifest as the
          path-independent cocycle of unresolved operational distinctions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Sharp falsifiers</p>
        <h2>Break descent or refinement coherence</h2>
        <p>
          The proposal fails if a claimed distinction is invisible to every physical effect, if
          entropy changes under presentation-only refinement, or if two source-derived refinement
          paths between the same outcome objects yield incompatible conditional states.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Prohibited overclaim</p>
        <h2>No row-count ontology</h2>
        <p>
          Entity counts, term counts, and graph decompositions are not entropy. The analogy does
          not establish digital physics, observer-created reality, or a literal database beneath
          spacetime. Operational distinguishability remains a derived physical condition.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <article class="frontier-card frontier-card--gap" aria-labelledby="datomic-context-title">
      <header>
        <p>Speculation 04 · immutable identity and contextual value</p>
        <span>conjectural</span>
      </header>
      <h2 id="datomic-context-title">A Datomic-like substrate with noncommuting materializations</h2>
      <p>
        Datomic’s separation of identity, immutable value, and transaction history suggests a
        sharper metaphysical analogy. Marici may preserve labelled identity and provenance while
        allowing sector or measurement contexts to materialize different coherent values. The
        proposed extension beyond Datomic is essential: valid physical views may be mutually
        noncommuting and therefore may not embed into one globally joinable classical value.
      </p>
    </article>

    <div class="dimension-grid" aria-label="Status and tests for the Datomic contextual-value speculation">
      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Established pressure</p>
        <h2>Context overlap is not an ordinary join</h2>
        <p>
          In both scattering and flavor, each projector family is internally commutative, distinct
          physical families have nonzero cross-commutators, and their trace-overlap matrices are
          positive and bistochastic.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Conjectural step</p>
        <h2>Identity may persist across incompatible values</h2>
        <p>
          The Carrier may generate enduring identities, transformation provenance, and the family
          of contexts in which compatible facts can become definite—without supplying one master
          classical record containing every contextual value.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Sharp falsifier</p>
        <h2>Locate the source of noncommutativity</h2>
        <p>
          The strong conjecture fails if the noncommuting context family enters only through
          sector-specific Hilbert-space input and cannot be reconstructed from Carrier operations,
          incidence, transport, and physical selection.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Prohibited identifications</p>
        <h2>Context is not database time</h2>
        <p>
          A quantum context is not an <code>as-of</code> value, transport is not transaction
          history, and incompatibility is not eventual-consistency lag. Datomic supplies an
          architectural analogy, not a physical reduction.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <article class="frontier-card frontier-card--gap" aria-labelledby="instrument-surface-title">
      <header>
        <p>Speculation 05 · capability and interaction</p>
        <span>conjectural</span>
      </header>
      <h2 id="instrument-surface-title">The physical surface may be a capability-indexed instrument UI</h2>
      <p>
        “Readout” may be too passive. A physical interaction can expose a classical record and
        transform the state available to subsequent interactions. The candidate surface therefore
        contains read-only effects, authorized preparations and channels, public records, and
        stronger diagnostic or side-channel capabilities.
      </p>
    </article>

    <div class="dimension-grid" aria-label="Status and tests for the instrument-surface speculation">
      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Established pressure</p>
        <h2>Equal output can hide unequal backaction</h2>
        <p>
          The established scattering and flavor effects admit exact, repeatable formal instrument
          completions. Direct coarse and fine-then-forget completions can return the same
          probability while preserving versus erasing hidden coherence. Neither source currently
          selects those state-update maps physically.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Conjectural step</p>
        <h2>The sector may generate an affordance surface</h2>
        <p>
          A sector may co-generate what can be queried, what can be changed, which capabilities are
          available, which records are public, and which stronger interactions expose internal
          organization.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Sharp falsifier</p>
        <h2>Derive the capability lattice</h2>
        <p>
          The strong claim fails if preparations, effects, state-update channels, and the
          public-versus-diagnostic boundary cannot be typed through Carrier operations and must all
          be supplied independently by sector physics.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="dimension-card">
        <p class="dimension-role">Prohibited overclaim</p>
        <h2>Observable is broader than public UI</h2>
        <p>
          A measurable side channel is not automatically a semantic surface property. Nor does
          “write” mean arbitrary mutation: every intervention remains constrained by physical
          resources, causal access, support, and source authorization.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="snapshot-callout" aria-labelledby="status-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Epistemic boundary</p>
      <h2 id="status-title">Why keep this outside the Frontier Atlas?</h2>
      <p>
        The Atlas versions what the evidence currently supports. Speculations organize possible
        explanations of that evidence. A speculation may graduate only after its claimed functors,
        naturality squares, and falsifiers become source-typed tests.
      </p>
    </section>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
